        <headline>High Surf Advisory issued September 24 at 2:23PM EDT until September 27 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Gray ME</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Large breaking waves of 7 to 12 feet and a high risk of
rip currents.

* WHERE...In Maine, Coastal York, Coastal Cumberland, Sagadahoc,
Lincoln and Knox Counties. In New Hampshire, Coastal
Rockingham County.

* WHEN...From 8 AM Friday to 8 PM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Dangerous swimming and surfing conditions and
localized beach erosion.
</description>
        <instruction>Inexperienced swimmers should remain out of the water due to
dangerous surf conditions.</instruction>
